1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Choose the cyclone forecast scenario to begin the voyage demo.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Run the optimizer to compare fuel, cost, emissions, and risk.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000
The balanced plan lowers fuel and CO₂e, with shore power at berth.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Replay the voyage and watch the vessel follow its planned corridor.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
At T+36 hours, the forecast shifts south and storm risk increases.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,000
A rolling re-plan generates a safer weather-routed corridor from the live position.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Arrival confirms the final fuel, CO₂e, risk, distance, and ETA.

8
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Results compares the Pareto trade-offs: balanced, lowest-cost, fastest, and baseline.

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Fleet opens the vessel dossier, including hull, engine, cargo, and CII details.

10
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Routes shows the mission builder, fuel choices, priorities, and search registration.

11
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Analytics explains prediction quality, convergence, Pareto performance, and cost.

12
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Ports checks channel limits, vessel compatibility, and operational constraints.

13
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Settings controls units, safety thresholds, accounting, replay, and algorithms.
